Cell[TextData[{
 "Create new features (using the features described in Question 1)  to create \
a non-linear model for this problem.\nAlso, state how you split the data up \
for this model.\n",
 StyleBox["Answer:\n",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0., 0., 1.]],
 StyleBox["For the non-linear model  I created new features from the previous \
features in question 1. I then generated additional polynomial features by \
squaring the existing numerical features, allowing the model to identify \
non-linear relationships between house characteristics and their sale prices.\
\nThe features were normalized using Z-score normalization to keep them on a \
similar scale. I split the available labelled data into 80% training data and \
20% testing data. The training data was used to train the polynomial \
regression model, while the testing data was kept separate to evaluate how \
well the model predicts house prices it has not seen before.",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0]]
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8406077677898483`*^9, 3.8406077805787115`*^9}, {
   3.840607817148863*^9, 3.8406078233314943`*^9}, {3.840610140231086*^9, 
   3.8406101687976065`*^9}, {3.8406102442374554`*^9, 3.840610249879386*^9}, {
   3.8406104763159466`*^9, 3.840610476396017*^9}, {3.8406115539824295`*^9, 
   3.840611557895995*^9}, {3.8406117070059996`*^9, 3.840611716240615*^9}, {
   3.840611795037814*^9, 3.840611800689047*^9}, 3.840619913048134*^9, {
   3.840619945716013*^9, 3.8406199457900066`*^9}, {3.8406200675701847`*^9, 
   3.840620069959527*^9}, 3.840620205383778*^9, {3.840623638351478*^9, 
   3.8406236387104607`*^9}, 3.840623699612303*^9, {3.9412712524564915`*^9, 
   3.941271393750354*^9}, {3.941271450684078*^9, 3.9412715211750045`*^9}, {
   3.96813379666777*^9, 3.9681337973066034`*^9}, {3.9681338728926716`*^9, 
   3.9681339384197025`*^9}, 3.968133979435996*^9, {3.9681340230173388`*^9, 
   3.9681340375069027`*^9}, {4.0040936147666187`*^9, 
