   3.8474384957971125`*^9, {3.903686603551216*^9, 3.903686618911228*^9}, {
   3.9681337054668045`*^9, 3.968133705562128*^9}, {3.96813395401865*^9, 
   3.968133954125353*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6a45d7a3-bf6e-46bc-b91a-\
a1d8014e34f0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "State how well the non-linear model performed (explaining your reasoning) \
and compare it to the linear model.\n",
 StyleBox["Answer:",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0., 0., 1.]]
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8406077677898483`*^9, 3.8406077805787115`*^9}, {
   3.840607817148863*^9, 3.8406078233314943`*^9}, {3.840610140231086*^9, 
   3.8406101687976065`*^9}, {3.8406102722419147`*^9, 3.840610312311409*^9}, {
   3.840610488985128*^9, 3.840610492835432*^9}, {3.8406115632144876`*^9, 
   3.840611566794153*^9}, {3.8406117273500357`*^9, 3.840611735133881*^9}, {
   3.840619975800766*^9, 3.8406199830796323`*^9}, {3.840620082988729*^9, 
   3.84062008898042*^9}, {3.8406216718281384`*^9, 3.8406217115710506`*^9}, {
   3.8406217827952547`*^9, 3.8406217834132743`*^9}, {3.840623666882721*^9, 
   3.8406236672154307`*^9}, 3.840623703349069*^9, {3.9681341681695957`*^9, 
   3.9681341956673574`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"bbd39193-8b8d-46a4-b448-\
cf6bbac66c47"],

Cell["\<\


To evaluate how well the non-linear regression model performed. We compare it \
against the linear regression model using Mean Squared Error (MSE), Root Mean \
Squared Error (RMSE) and R Squared (R\.b2).
The R\.b2 results show that the linear model explained approximately 59.56% \
of the variation in house prices, while the polynomial model explained \
approximately 64.43%. The polynomial model also reduced the RMSE by \
approximately 6.22%, meaning its predictions had smaller errors overall.
The polynomial model performed better because it included the squared values \
of the original features. This allowed it to capture non-linear relationships \
between house characteristics and sale prices that the linear model could not \
represent.
However, the polynomial model still had a relatively high RMSE, meaning some \
predictions were still quite far from the actual prices. This could be \
because other important house characteristics were not included in the model.
Overall, the polynomial regression model performed better than the linear \
regression model on the testing dataset, although there is still room for \
improvement.
\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8406077657661633`*^9, 3.8406077988842287`*^9}, {
  3.8406214832776375`*^9, 3.840621485297165*^9}, {4.004198920020817*^9, 
  4.0041989257308426`*^9}, {4.00419916369261*^9, 
  4.0041992196031437`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"a353913f-d856-40c0-a522-\
51f0838fc1de"],

Cell["Code used to produce answer:", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8406212671583977`*^9, 3.840621294907153*^9}, {
  3.840623759650882*^9, 3.8406237597957306`*^9}},
 FontWeight->"Bold",
 FontColor->RGBColor[
  0., 0., 1.],ExpressionUUID->"9af1e54b-3b2f-486e-8c0e-2bfa9a62276b"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"xTrainLinear", "=", 
   RowBox[{"Map", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Prepend", "[", 
       RowBox[{"#", ",", "1"}], "]"}], "&"}], ",", "xTrainScaled"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"xTestLinear", "=", 
    RowBox[{"Map", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Prepend", "[", 
        RowBox[{"#", ",", "1"}], "]"}], "&"}], ",", "xTestScaled"}], "]"}]}], 
   ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"thetaLinear", "=", 
    RowBox[{"LeastSquares", "[", 
     RowBox[{"xTrainLinear", ",", "yTrain"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], 
  "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\n", 
  RowBox[{"(*", 
   RowBox[{"Predict", " ", "house", " ", "prices"}], "*)"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"predictionsLinear", "=", 
   RowBox[{"xTestLinear", ".", "thetaLinear"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"predictionsPoly", "=", 
    RowBox[{"xTestPoly", ".", "thetaPoly"}]}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  "\n", 
  RowBox[{"(*", 
   RowBox[{
   "Calculate", " ", "Linear", " ", "Regression", " ", "performance"}], 
   "*)"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"mseLinear", "=", 
   RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"yTest", "-", "predictionsLinear"}], ")"}], "^", "2"}], "]"}]}],
   ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"rmseLinear", "=", 
    RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "mseLinear", "]"}]}], ";"}], 
  "\[IndentingNewLine]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"rSquaredLinear", "=", 
    RowBox[{"1", "-", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"yTest", "-", "predictionsLinear"}], ")"}], "^", "2"}], 
       "]"}], "/", 
      RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"yTest", "-", 
          RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "yTest", "]"}]}], ")"}], "^", "2"}], 
       "]"}]}]}]}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\n", 
  RowBox[{"(*", 
   RowBox[{
   "Calculate", " ", "Polynomial", " ", "Regression", " ", "performance"}], 
   "*)"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"msePoly", "=", 
   RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"yTest", "-", "predictionsPoly"}], ")"}], "^", "2"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"rmsePoly", "=", 
    RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "msePoly", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"rSquaredPoly", "=", 
    RowBox[{"1", "-", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"yTest", "-", "predictionsPoly"}], ")"}], "^", "2"}], "]"}], 
      "/", 
      RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
